%I A400672 #17 Oct 04 2026 15:42:10
%S A400672 0,1,1,2,4,14,211,36672,3066802890
%N A400672 Number of equivalence classes of monotone Boolean functions of n variables that contain their duals.
%C A400672 Two monotone Boolean functions are equivalent if one is obtained from the other by a permutation of the variables. Then a(n) is the number of equivalence classes [f] such that D(f) belongs to [f], where D(f)(x) = 1 - f(1 - x).
%C A400672 For the identity permutation, the functions f satisfying f = D(f) are the self-dual monotone Boolean functions, counted by A001206.
%F A400672 a(n) = 2*A003183(n) - A003182(n).
%F A400672 a(n) = (1/n!)*Sum_{sigma in S_n} |{f in M_n : f = sigma D(f)}|, where M_n is the set of monotone Boolean functions on n labeled variables.
%e A400672 For n = 2, the only equivalence class that is equivalent to its dual is the class containing f(x_1,x_2) = x_1 (and, by permutation, x_2). Hence a(2) = 1.
%Y A400672 Cf. A000372, A001206 (self-dual monotone Boolean functions), A003182 (equivalence under permutations), A003183 (equivalence under permutations and duality).
%K A400672 nonn,more,new
%O A400672 0,4
